  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.5.3\n            \n            RoomSharp v0.5.3 is an ecosystem alignment release.\n            Starting with v0.5.3, RoomSharp uses synchronized versioning across ecosystem packages. Packages released as part of the same ecosystem update now share the same version number.\n            RoomSharp is a multi-package ecosystem. Patch releases may stabilize generator, runtime, provider, CLI, and extension behavior together. Feature releases are followed by short stabilization cycles.\n            Recommendation: keep all RoomSharp packages on the same version when using multiple packages together.\n\n            v0.5.2\n\n            Highlights:\n            - [SoftDelete] generated DAO restore/hard-delete methods now live directly on DAO implementations.\n            - [SoftDelete] DAO [Query] methods now auto-filter deleted rows at prepare-time.\n            - [Encrypted] properties are now automatically decrypted after generated SELECT queries.\n            - [Auditable] entities now auto-populate CreatedAt/UpdatedAt and support IAuditContext user tracking.\n\n            Generated Code & Performance:\n            - Parallel generated DAOs now use DbSession.GetOrCreateCommand(...) instead of shared DbCommand state.\n            - Serialized generated DAOs now use shared DaoHelpers for transaction normalization, cached commands, and cloned-command disposal.\n            - Reduced generated allocation/disposal overhead across DAO and DatabaseImpl code paths.\n            - Insert generation now avoids unnecessary SQL Server fallback delegate allocations when fallback cannot run.\n            - Relation loading caches column metadata and validates relation definitions earlier.\n            - PagingSource now supports native async loaders with cancellation.\n\n            Fixes:\n            - Fixed GlobalFilter parameter binding in parallel generated SELECT queries.\n            - Fixed QueryCache.InvalidateByPrefix() to return int as expected by QueryExtensions.\n            - Fixed [Auditable] code generation to call IAuditContext.GetCurrentUser().\n            - Fixed soft-delete generated SQL/parameter caching consistency in parallel mode.\n            - Hardened ConnectionPool, bulk insert cleanup, migration lock release, ObservableQuery cancellation, FTS SQL quoting, and legacy query cache behavior.\n\n            Docs & Coverage:\n            - Added README coverage for GlobalFilters and other previously undocumented features.\n            - Added generator/runtime tests covering soft-delete caching, serialized helper usage, insert fallback rules, GlobalFilter parameter binding, infrastructure cleanup, relation metadata, paging cancellation, and cache single-flight behavior.",
